       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 600 mg daily is three times the FDA maximum of 200 mg/day, and I don't see a reason to exceed that limit in a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function. At that dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, seizures, and QT prolongation.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n\n- **50 mg daily**, a typical starting dose\n- **100 mg daily**\n- **200 mg daily**, the maximum\n- **60 mg daily**, if the 0 was a typo\n\nIf you really do want 600 mg, for example as part of a specific protocol or a toxicology plan, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it's intentional. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
